## Sample / filter accounting
- NLSY79 raw: 12,686 rows.
- "Height 1981" column: ALL 12,143 non-null values fall 400–611 — not inches; ignored entirely.
- "Height 1985" column (inches): 10,863 usable (1,823 respondents excluded for no plausible height).
- BMI computations: weight(lbs) × 703 / height(1985, in)².
- Pre-plausibility-filter group n for composite at BMI 1989: n0 = 9,086, n1 = 1,107.
- Post-plausibility-filter (BMI in [12, 80]): n0 = 9,074, n1 = 1,107.

## Unit / data anomalies (fixed, not silently)
- Weights treated as POUNDS (dataset description says kg; using kg gave infeasible BMI).
- Height 1981 column dropped (code is corrupted or mis-scaled).
- Savings-direction variable is already categorical (1/2/3/4 as documented).
- Wealth 1990 winsorized at [1st, 99th] before residualization on age/sex/race.

## Hypothesis (associational, paste-ready)
Among NLSY79 respondents with non-missing 1985 height, 1989 savings, and 1990 wealth, an "impatience-leaning" profile — defined as having 1989 self-reported savings direction equal to "took money out" or "no savings" AND falling in the bottom quintile of 1990 family net wealth (residualized on age, sex, and race) — is associated with higher 1989 BMI (adjusted coefficient +0.68 BMI units, 95% CI [+0.35, +1.02], p < 0.001), after controlling for age, sex, race, log family income in 1985, and respondent's own highest grade completed. The savings-direction-only signal shows a consistent positive association of smaller magnitude (adjusted +0.47, 95% CI [+0.27, +0.68]). Cause cannot be inferred from this cross-sectional observational analysis.

## Failure modes honestly reported
- 4,327 of 12,686 respondents (34%) have no 1985 height, so no BMI can be computed for them — most attrition is structural, not analytic.
- Composite-impatience flag depends on having non-missing savings direction AND 1990 wealth, so its effective n is ~10,000–11,000 even pre-filter.
- Effect is small in absolute terms (~0.5–1.0 BMI units) — clinically modest noise on individual level, but consistent direction across waves and specifications.

